<title>FRANCE: French capacity use slightly higher -survey.</title>
<headline>French capacity use slightly higher -survey.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>French capacity utilisation has risen slightly, national statistics institute INSEE said in its quarterly survey of business leaders, carried out in January.</p>
<p>It gave the following data on capacity utilisation rates (in percentages) broken down by sector:</p>
<p>			    97   96    96    96   96   95    95   95</p>
<p>			    Jan  Oct   Jul   Apr  Jan  Oct   Jul  Apr</p>
<p> Industry overall     83.0 82.3  82.7  83.8 83.6 84.2  84.8 84.8</p>
<p> Manufacturing	  82.6 82.1  82.4  83.6 83.5 84.2  84.4 84.6</p>
<p> Agri-business	  81.9 81.3  80.7  79.9 79.9 81.9  82.2 80.8</p>
<p> Semi-finished goods  84.3 84.6  85.5  85.5 85.1 86.0  88.4 87.7</p>
<p> Capital goods	  82.4 81.6  82.1  82.3 82.4 84.1  81.2 82.5</p>
<p> Cars, land transport 82.1 80.4  80.6  87.0 85.7 84.3  84.7 86.1</p>
<p> Consumer goods	 81.1 81.0  80.4  80.7 81.3 82.2  82.9 82.5</p>
<p> Energy		   93.1 87.2  93.7  99.7 96.4 90.6 100.0 99.7</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5071</p>
</text>
